### Describe the bug

I want to use a "suspended" query in combination with `next-auth`. 

For this I created a `protectedProcedure` like this:

```ts
const isAuthed = t.middleware(({ ctx, next }) => {
  if (!ctx.session || !ctx.session.user) {
    throw new TRPCError({ code: "UNAUTHORIZED" });
  }
  return next({
    ctx: {
      // infers the `session` as non-nullable
      session: { ...ctx.session, user: ctx.session.user },
    },
  });
});

export const protectedProcedure = t.procedure.use(isAuthed);
```

and am using it in my router:

```ts
getSecretMessage: protectedProcedure.query(() => {
    return "you can now see this secret message!";
}),
```

My expectation would be that this query gets authorized even with `{suspense: true}` which is unfortunately not the case. 
Using it without suspense returns the correct data and I have a session in in my context.

```ts
const { data: secretMessage } = trpc.auth.getSecretMessage.useQuery(
    undefined, // no input
  );
```

As soon as I add the `suspense` flag it is not working anymore and the session is always null which results in an unauthorized error

```ts
const { data: secretMessage } = trpc.auth.getSecretMessage.useQuery(
      undefined, // no input
      {suspense: true}
  );
```
It is the same behaviour with `useSuspenseQuery`.


### Link to reproduction

https://github.com/engelkes-finstreet/next-auth-trpc-suspense

### To reproduce

Unfortunately I could not get the example running on Stackblitz / Codesandbox so I hope a link to my GitHub-Repository is enough as well.

Check out the repository and add any provider inside `pages/api/auth/[...nextauth].ts` and add these credentials to a `.env` file. You can copy the `.env.example` for it. Afterwards run `npx prisma migrate dev` and start the dev server with `npm run dev`. 
On the index page is a `sign in` button which you can click and sign in with your given provider. After the redirect back to the index page try to refresh the page and you will see that the authorization error occurs. 
Now you can go ahead and remove the `{ suspense: true }` from the query and refresh the page. Now you will see the secret message.

